ate":0.6842,"pass_rate_neutral":0.6087,"def_epa_per_play":-0.287},{"week":5,"opponent":"BUF","home":true,"pf":34.0,"pa":37.0,"off_snaps":79,"epa_per_play":0.2306,"pass_rate":0.7089,"pass_rate_neutral":0.7,"def_epa_per_play":0.2914},{"week":6,"opponent":"ARI","home":true,"pf":16.0,"pa":18.0,"off_snaps":57,"epa_per_play":-0.1551,"pass_rate":0.6491,"pass_rate_neutral":0.6087,"def_epa_per_play":-0.0206}],"comps":{"offense":[{"season":2022,"team":"MIN","distance":0.7105,"shared":12,"play_caller":"Kevin O'Connell"},{"season":2023,"team":"SEA","distance":0.7185,"shared":12,"play_caller":null},{"season":2025,"team":"DAL","distance":0.8191,"shared":12,"play_caller":"Brian Schottenheimer"},{"season":2025,"team":"JAX","distance":0.8207,"shared":12,"play_caller":"Liam Coen"},{"season":2024,"team":"HOU","distance":0.8233,"shared":12,"play_caller":"Bobby Slowik"}],"defense":[{"season":2024,"team":"CIN","distance":0.2007,"shared":4,"play_caller":"Lou Anarumo"},{"season":2023,"team":"KC","distance":0.2449,"shared":4,"play_caller":"Steve Spagnuolo"},{"season":2022,"team":"CLE","distance":0.2513,"shared":4,"play_caller":null},{"season":2025,"team":"NE","distance":0.2571,"shared":4,"play_caller":null},{"season":2022,"team":"DAL","distance":0.2675,"shared":4,"play_caller":"Dan Quinn"}]},"overview":{"overview":"The Rams are 2-4 through week 6 of the 2026 season and have been outscored 138 to 135. Both sides of the ball have been strong, with the offense 10th in EPA per play and the defense 10th in EPA allowed. The record undersells them so far, since teams with numbers like these usually win more often. What sets them apart is the 3rd highest early-down pass rate in the league.","offense":"The Rams offense has been well above average by EPA per play so far. Their run and pass mix has stayed close to what game situations call for. Their biggest outliers in how they line up are the 2nd lowest RPO rate in the league. Matthew Stafford has run the passing game, with Puka Nacua leading the team in targets.","defense":"The Rams defense has been well above average by EPA allowed per play so far. Its strongest area has been EPA allowed per play, where it ranks 10th, and its weakest has been sack rate, where it ranks 28th. Byron Young has led the way with 3.5 sacks. Their scheme has been fairly conventional, and the closest thing to a signature is an eight man box rate that ranks 12th highest in the league.","special":"The Rams have been about average in how often they go for it on fourth down. Their kickers have made 60% of field goals, which is the worst in the league. On the roster side, they put an unusually large share of their salary cap into the secondary, about 24% of the money on the books. Their offensive line was among the oldest in the league.","players":"Matthew Stafford has played nearly every snap at quarterback and thrown for 1,794 yards. Targets have been spread around, with Puka Nacua and Davante Adams leading a group where nobody has more than a fifth of the looks. Kyren Williams has handled most of the work in the backfield with 59% of the carries. On defense, Byron Young leads the team with 3.5 sacks and Quentin Lake has picked off 2 passes.","coaching":"Sean McVay is calling the offense as head coach and Chris Shula is calling the defense. Their offense looks most like the 2022 Vikings under Kevin O'Connell and the 2023 Seahawks. Their defense looks most like the 2024 Bengals under Lou Anarumo and the 2023 Chiefs under Steve Spagnuolo.","trends":"The offense went from 2nd in EPA per play in 2025 to 10th so far this season, a big step back. The defense moved from 9th in EPA allowed per play in 2025 to 10th so far this season, about where it was. The biggest change in approach was two point attempt rate, which went from 0% to 12%.","notes":"The 2026 pages are built from data that nflverse updates every week, so they will keep changing until the season ends. Personnel, formations, coverage and pressure numbers are missing for now because that data is only released after the season."}}